    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Green-Bay-WI/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Quantitative-Psychology_JR10015436": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Applied Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Teaching Professor - Applied Psychology Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Teaching Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Psychology Department invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor of Psychology to join a student-centered academic community committed to teaching excellence, access, and student success. In alignment with UW-Green Bay’s mission to fearlessly meet challenges, embrace diversity, care for the region, and provide educational opportunity for all, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in multiple modalities, including Psychopathology/Abnormal Psychology, Counseling and Psychotherapy, Theories of Counseling, Counseling Microskills, and additional courses within their area of expertise. This position offers the opportunity to positively impact students through innovative, inclusive teaching practices that support learners from diverse, underrepresented, and first-generation backgrounds while advancing the University’s strategic priorities of student success, inclusivity, and community connection. As a valued member of the Psychology faculty, the successful candidate will contribute to a collaborative and engaged academic environment through student mentoring, shared governance, professional development, and departmental service. We seek an educator who embodies UW-Green Bay’s core values by advancing fearlessly, empowering success, provisioning access, building community, and expressing gratitude. Join a university on the rise where learning extends beyond the classroom, community impact matters, and together we create opportunities for students, strengthen Northeast Wisconsin, and fulfill our commitment 